    <string name="security_section_title">About Security</string>
    <string name="security_description">Your ECS-ID and password are sent directly to Kyoto University\'s authentication server (auth.iimc.kyoto-u.ac.jp) through the in-app WebView. Your credentials are never sent to the KULMS+ developer\'s server.\n\nIf you save your password on this device, it is protected by AES-256 encryption (managed by AndroidKeyStore). Your TOTP secret key is also encrypted and stored in the same way.\n\nNote: Storing both your password and TOTP secret on the same device means both authentication factors are on one device. For maximum security, consider using a separate authenticator app (e.g. Google Authenticator) on another device.\n\nThe source code for this app is available on GitHub, so anyone can verify how credentials are handled.</string>
